    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T17:19:40Z",
    "body": "The maintainer asked for this work on 2026-11-19. His words: \"So then its time to throw out stepio from truck and finalize the switch to solidcore\".\n\nLabel changes:\n\n- `P6` becomes `P4`, because the maintainer asked for the work in his own words.\n- `blocked` is removed. The block was #916 (the solidcore STEP bench). #916 is closed and shipped in v0.19.0. Nothing else blocks this issue.\n\nScope, as the maintainer set it today:\n\n- The STEP import of the app goes through the solidcore importer behind the kernel seam.\n- `truck-stepio` and `ruststep` leave `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`. truck stays only where code that is not STEP import needs it. This replaces \"`truck-*` leaves\" in the issue body.\n- The import behaviour in the UI and the CLI stays: the error text, the refusal of corrupt input, and no crash.\n- The solidcore pin moves to `2016386442dfee3b2a0c3a1bfdd4017c5254dac8` in this work (#2781).\n- #2780 (a legal file with a twisted B-spline flank is refused) must close with this switch if the new importer reads such a face. A STEP fixture that we make ourselves confirms it.\n\nThe work starts after the gate of PR #2773 and the process bump. Only one local build runs at a time.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
