    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T17:26:49Z",
    "body": "Maintainer direction (relayed by the main session, 2026-11-19): the app uses solidcore for all STEP reading. No second STEP path stays.\n\nScope that this adds to the issue:\n\n- Port each reader that uses `ruststep` to the `solidcore-step` parser. These are the five readers outside the importer:\n  - `step_csys.rs` (the tool-body coordinate reader, used by the `tool_body*` commands)\n  - `step_closed.rs`\n  - `step_diag.rs`\n  - `step_units.rs`\n  - `step_depth.rs`\n- Remove `truck-stepio` and `ruststep` fully from each `Cargo.toml` and from `Cargo.lock`. Remove the `[patch.crates-io]` entry for `ruststep` too.\n- Keep `truck` only where code that does not read STEP needs it.\n- Keep the import behaviour of the UI and the CLI: the error text, the refusal on corrupt input, no crash and no hang.\n\nSplit rule:\n\n- If the work is too large for one PR, the worker splits it into stacked PRs.\n- The PRs are worked one at a time. Each PR has its own gate.\n- Each part gets a sub-issue under this issue, with `P3`. The sub-issues are worked in the bug lane.\n\nThe solidcore pin move of #2781 stays a part of this work. #2780 closes with it only if a fixture that we make ourselves confirms the result.\n",
