    "body": "The worker split the work into three stacked PRs. They are worked one at a time, each with its own gate.\n\n1. Part 1, branch `issue/917-solidcore-step` (`Refs #917`): the solidcore pin move of #2781, the STEP importer through `camcraft_geometry::step` to the kernel, the removal of the truck helper modules from the app. The code is written. It is not built yet: only one build runs on the machine at a time.\n2. Part 2, #2789: the tool coordinate reader, the units reader and the depth check use the `solidcore-step` parser. `ruststep` leaves the app.\n3. Part 3, #2790: `truck-stepio` and `ruststep` leave the workspace and the kernel bench. Its PR closes this issue.\n\nOpen risk for part 1: at the old pin, solidcore refused four tracked fixtures (`fig8.step`, `fillet_corner.step`, `bar_cross_holes.step`, `bspline_discontinuous.step`). The first build shows if the new pin reads them. If it does not, part 1 cannot merge as planned, and the finding comes here.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
