    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T18:25:22Z",
    "body": "Finding from the first build of part 1: the new solidcore pin (`2016386442dfee3b2a0c3a1bfdd4017c5254dac8`) refuses three tracked fixtures that the truck importer reads. Part 1 is stopped. No test was weakened and no fixture was changed.\n\nReadings from the kernel bench (`crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`, debug):\n\n| Fixture | solidcore at the new pin | truck |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fig8.step` | refused at read: pcurves failed on 1 of 30 faces: `not supported yet: no exact pcurve of a NURBS on a spline surface` | reads, V=136543.72 |\n| `fillet_corner.step` | refused at read: pcurves failed on 1 of 10 faces, same reason | reads, V=20651.68 |\n| `bar_cross_holes.step` | refused at read: pcurves failed on 3 of 7 faces: `no exact pcurve of a B-spline on a spline surface` | reads, V=45816.21 |\n| `bspline_discontinuous.step` | refused (pcurve of a line on a spline surface) | refused too: no change |\n| `twisted_flank.step` (our own fixture for #2780) | reads, 1 solid, V=8000.000000, watertight | open shell, V=0 |\n| `Milling-test.step`, `Milling-test-inch.step` | the bounding box now agrees (#939) | - |\n\nEach other tracked fixture keeps its verdict.\n\nResult: the switch of the app importer changes three fixtures from import to refusal. That is a regression, so part 1 cannot merge as planned. The cause is in solidcore: it has no exact pcurve of a NURBS or B-spline curve on a spline surface.\n\nThe new pin needs one build fix in the kernel: `brep::Surface` has a new `Blend` variant (`crates/kernel/src/mesh_bound.rs`, `mesh_deviation.rs`).\n\nHeld work: branch `issue/917-solidcore-step`, commit 776ba8b76548e3094a13534a0325332c69473039. It is not gated and has no PR.\n\nThe decision how to continue is with the maintainer. #2789 and #2790 wait for it.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
