    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T18:44:54Z",
    "body": "First build of the kernel part (branch `issue/2781-solidcore-pin-trims`, not pushed, not gated). The kernel now reads through `read_solids_with` with its own `Trims` kernel, after the pattern of the maintainer's Solidcraft.\n\nReadings (volume in mm³):\n\n| Fixture | solidcore exact | solidcore closed mesh | truck |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `fig8.step` | 136537.37 | 136541.45 | 136543.72 (agrees) |\n| `fillet_corner.step` | 26816.49 | 26815.46 | 20651.68, open mesh, 121 open edges |\n| `bar_cross_holes.step` | 78225.68 | 78218.79 | 45816.21, open mesh, 1090 open edges |\n| `twisted_flank.step` (ours) | 8000.000 | watertight | 0, open mesh |\n\nThe three fixtures now read through solidcore.\n\nDecisions (coordinator, recorded in `docs/decisions/917-kernel-pcurves.md` on the branch):\n\n1. `fillet_corner.step` and `bar_cross_holes.step` do not agree with the volumes of truck. The truck volumes come from open meshes, so they are not valid volumes. The bench rows say \"disagree\" and name the open edges as the cause. A new kernel test pins the solidcore volume against its own closed mesh and against a closed-form value, not against truck. No verdict on `main` is loosened: the two rows were \"solidcore refuses\".\n2. `bspline_discontinuous.step` reads with the new trims: V=1.125, with three edges up to 0.375 mm off their surfaces, and its closed mesh gives 1.068. That is a risk of a silent wrong solid. The fixture stays refused by name: the trims kernel refuses a face whose edge gap is over a tight limit. The limit comes from the measured gaps of the good fixtures. The bench row and a kernel test pin the refusal.\n\nFinding about the old path: the truck importer reads `fillet_corner.step` and `bar_cross_holes.step` as open meshes. The importer switch removes this defect.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
