    "body": "PR B (the importer switch) is on hold. The narrow gate on the local head 853de1685 (origin/main merged) has 18 red steps of 108. The kernel and geometry steps are green.\n\nTracked fixtures that truck read and that the solidcore path now refuses or reads differently:\n- `fillet_corner.step`: refused. \"face Some(1) stands 2.366e-2 mm off its surface, tolerance 5e-3 mm\".\n- `sample_ap214.step`: reads as non-manifold. The slicer refuses it (\"surfaces meet 3 or more ways\").\n- `box.step` with reversed faces: refused (\"encloses volume -1 mm^3\"). truck turned it outward.\n- The bore gouge pins (`bore_facet_sagitta`, `step_chord_units`) and the toolpath pins on fig8 and the user parts (`wall_arc_entry`, `lead_approach`, `shoulder_adaptive`) give different results.\n- Error texts changed in `step_nesting` and `import.rs`. A discontinuous edge curve now meshes and is not refused.\n\nThese are reader and mesher results, not test text. No pin is changed without the coordinator's word. The held work stays in the local worktree `issue-917`. Nothing is pushed.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
