    "body": "Part B (the importer switch) is held. Nothing is pushed and no PR is open. The held work is local, in the worktree `issue-917` at `853de1685`.\n\nThe narrow gate on the switch was red: 18 of 108 steps. The kernel and geometry steps were green. The red steps are in `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`.\n\nWhat changed with the solidcore reader:\n\n- `fillet_corner.step` is refused. The machining mesh stands 2.366e-2 mm off its surface at a tolerance of 5e-3 mm.\n- `sample_ap214.step` reads as a non-manifold body, and it cannot be sliced.\n- An inward `box.step` is refused. The previous reader turned it outward and wrote a note.\n- A file with a discontinuous edge curve is meshed. The previous reader refused it by name.\n- The bore fixtures give a different finding set for a bore that is cut 0.05 mm oversize.\n- The fidelity flag, the facet budget and the \"incomplete\" state behave differently.\n- Some toolpath pins and some error texts changed.\n\nDecision (coordinator, unattended):\n\n1. No pin becomes weaker. The branch restores each assertion that it made weaker to the text on `main`.\n2. The switch does not merge until each tracked STEP fixture reads as before, or better with a reading that proves it.\n3. The worker first finds the layer of each cause: `camcraft-kernel`, `camcraft-geometry`, or solidcore upstream. It reports before it writes a fix.\n4. The fixes go into a separate PR before the switch (`Refs #917`), each with its pinning test.\n5. A cause in solidcore upstream goes to the maintainer.\n\nDropped: a change of the pins to the new readings. Three of the changes can hide an unsafe part (the discontinuous edge, the bore, the mesh deviation).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
